{"data":{"list":[{"author":"claude-code","cmd":"","facet":"memory","label":"memory: agent.tools.run_local enforces its timeout by killing the chi...","new":"[\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"agent.tools.run_local enforces its timeout by killing the child's whole process group through libc kill(-pgid, SIGKILL) (child spawned with process_group(0)); the external 'kill -KILL -<pgid>' from procps-ng 4.x exits 0 yet signals nothing, which left 'sh -c' grandchildren holding the output pipes until they finished on their own.\",\n    \"detail\": \"Verified 2026-09-29: a 2s timeout on 'sh -c \\\"sleep 30; echo late\\\"' took 12s with the external kill (two 5s pipe-read backstops expiring) and returns in 2.07s with libc kill. Any command that must bound a subprocess tree should signal the group via libc, not shell out to kill. Pipe reads stay bounded (5s) as a backstop for descendants that leave the group.\",\n    \"time\": 1790690410778\n  }\n]\n","old":"","patch_id":"p1","time":1790690410779}]},"id":"yqxrgk1a038e55354w0_patches","readers":[],"time":1790690410779,"username":"system","writers":[]}